---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="TAROS — Runtime Monitoring for Autonomous Systems"
  description="TAROS, the Trusted Autonomous Runtime Oversight System, monitors autonomous systems and AI/SI agents as they run, and records every decision with its reason."
  current="home"
>
  <!-- 1. Hero -->
  <section class="section section--hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="hero">
        <p class="hero__badge">Runtime Monitoring &amp; Oversight</p>
        <h1 class="hero__title">TAROS</h1>
        <p class="hero__subtitle">The Trusted Autonomous Runtime Oversight System. TAROS monitors your autonomous systems and AI/SI agents as they run, and records every decision with its reason.</p>
        <a href="/contact.html" class="hero__cta">Start the conversation</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!--
    TAROS intro animation: embedded via iframe.
    The animation is a self-contained HTML file (animations/taros_introduction.html) with
    its own CSS, scene markup (with embedded assets), and Web Speech API voice-over.
    Using an iframe keeps the main page small and avoids duplicating ~300KB of content
    and logic; the animation retains full play/pause/mute controls and works responsively
    inside the frame. We lazy-load the iframe when this section enters the viewport.
  -->
  <section class="section intro-animation" id="taros-intro" aria-labelledby="intro-animation-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="intro-animation__header">
        <h2 class="intro-animation__title" id="intro-animation-heading">TAROS intro</h2>
        <p class="intro-animation__desc">Watch a short animated overview of TAROS and how it monitors and oversees AI/SI systems while they run.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="intro-animation__wrapper">
        <div class="intro-animation__scale">
          <iframe
            class="intro-animation__iframe"
            title="TAROS animated introduction with voice-over"
            data-src="/animations/taros_introduction.html"
          ></iframe>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="intro-animation__hint">Use the controls inside the animation to play, pause, restart, or toggle voice-over. Buttons are keyboard-accessible.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2. What TAROS is -->
  <section class="section" id="what-is-taros">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <header class="section__header">
        <h2 class="section__title">What TAROS is</h2>
        <p class="section__intro lead">TAROS, the Trusted Autonomous Runtime Oversight System, monitors every autonomous system you connect while it runs.</p>
      </header>
      <p>Autonomous machines and AI/SI (Artificial Intelligence or Super Intelligence) agents report their events to TAROS. Each event is checked against signed, versioned policies, and TAROS returns allow, hold, or block, with the reason. Every decision is recorded, so you always know what your systems did and why.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3. Why runtime monitoring -->
  <section class="section section--alt" id="why-platform">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <header class="section__header">
        <h2 class="section__title">Why autonomous systems need runtime monitoring</h2>
        <p class="section__intro">Autonomous systems act at machine speed. Pre-deployment testing can’t show what they do in production. Continuous runtime monitoring can.</p>
      </header>
      <p>TAROS sits above your certified safety function and your autonomy stack. It monitors what your systems do, applies policies that no single person can change, and keeps a tamper-evident record of every decision—so oversight is continuous, not an afterthought.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4. What enterprises gain with TAROS -->
  <section class="section" id="what-you-gain">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="section__header">
        <h2 class="section__title">What enterprises gain with TAROS</h2>
        <p class="section__intro lead">Organizations adopting TAROS gain a clearer path to responsible AI/SI at scale.</p>
      </header>
      <ul class="gains-list">
        <li><strong>Continuous visibility</strong> — Know what your autonomous systems are doing, as they do it.</li>
        <li><strong>Stronger safety controls</strong> — Structured oversight and guardrails around AI/SI-driven systems.</li>
        <li><strong>Clearer governance and oversight</strong> — Policy alignment and visibility into how AI/SI behaves and makes decisions.</li>
        <li><strong>Reduced operational and regulatory risk</strong> — A foundation that supports compliance and audit readiness.</li>
        <li><strong>Confidence in deployment</strong> — Deploy AI/SI systems knowing that appropriate safeguards and governance structures are in place.</li>
        <li><strong>Trustworthy AI/SI operations</strong> — A platform built for safety, not just capability.</li>
        <li><strong>Readiness for responsible AI/SI at scale</strong> — From pilot to production with consistency and control.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5. Key Pillars / Benefits -->
  <section class="section section--alt" id="pillars">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="section__header">
        <h2 class="section__title">Key pillars</h2>
        <p class="section__intro">The capabilities that define runtime oversight for autonomous systems.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="pillars">
        <article class="pillar">
          <h3 class="pillar__title">Monitoring</h3>
          <p class="pillar__text">Watch every event from your autonomous systems as it happens, and evaluate it at runtime.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="pillar">
          <h3 class="pillar__title">Policy &amp; control</h3>
          <p class="pillar__text">Signed, versioned policies decide what is allowed, held, or blocked—and no single person can change them alone.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="pillar">
          <h3 class="pillar__title">Evidence &amp; audit</h3>
          <p class="pillar__text">Every decision is recorded with its explanation, ready for review and audit.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="pillar">
          <h3 class="pillar__title">Human authority</h3>
          <p class="pillar__text">Human oversight that is explicit, bounded, and enforceable—with independent approval for every policy change.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 6. Who TAROS is for -->
  <section class="section" id="who-its-for">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="section__header">
        <h2 class="section__title">Who TAROS is for</h2>
        <p class="section__intro lead">Built for teams that care about how AI/SI is deployed and operated.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="audience">
        <div class="audience__item">
          <strong>Enterprise leaders</strong>
          <span>Executives and decision-makers who need confidence in AI/SI adoption and risk management.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="audience__item">
          <strong>Platform &amp; engineering teams</strong>
          <span>Teams responsible for reliability and safe deployment of AI/SI-driven systems.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="audience__item">
          <strong>Safety &amp; governance leads</strong>
          <span>Those responsible for compliance, responsible AI/SI, and operational oversight.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 7. Trust-oriented CTA -->
  <section class="section" id="cta">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="cta-block">
        <h2 class="cta-block__title">Explore TAROS</h2>
        <p class="cta-block__text">Whether you are evaluating runtime monitoring for autonomous systems or building a roadmap for responsible AI/SI, we’d like to hear from you.</p>
        <a href="/contact.html" class="cta-block__link">Get in touch</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
